Okay, forgive me for abusing the spoiler system but ...

When you're aimlessly wandering around the dungeon don't use attack
commands to move (i.e. just don't do it). Instead use safe movement
sequences (they are documented on every platform). As an example, on
Unix you'll _never_ accidently hit a floating eye by typing <ctrl>move
keys. This is independent of load average and type ahead and what have
you. Okay, okay it would be unrealistic to expect that anyone might try
this because ... well I can't think of a good reason why anyone wouldn't
do this!

If your platform doesn't have this feature (safe movement sequences)
complain now!!!

